Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Build a Large Language Model from Scratch \[LongDash] in Wolfram Language\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"2c5ba7fd-8080-4cf7-9aa9-c487e995fc9c"],

Cell["\<\
Part 5: Sampling \[LongDash] greedy, temperature, top-k, top-p, beam, \
speculative\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"b2edaf89-f037-4499-9f73-612ffc520a92"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The trained model in Part 4 is, at every step, a function from a ",
 "context window to a length-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"bebf9c76-1dbe-49e1-a931-f9307d6919be"],
 " logit vector. ",
 StyleBox["Sampling",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " is the policy that turns those logits into a chosen next token. ",
 "Part 5 implements five strategies plus speculative decoding, all ",
 "from scratch, and shows what each does to the output distribution."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"419bc36c-2524-45d7-bda9-6113baafce9a"],

Cell["1.  Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"818aa2e3-6d8e-4fb3-a108-1989ba30ee76"],

Cell["SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"224ccb99-48b7-4462-a6ac-71e4b4aa6ac9"],

Cell["Get[\"src/Sampling.wl\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"04f9ae05-97fd-4178-840b-117a4d0f2f9c"],

Cell["2.  Temperature: the easiest dial", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e366a4b0-1e46-45b9-95e4-d727b81ec709"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The temperature scaling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"softmax", 
    RowBox[{"(", "logits"}]}], "/", "T", ")"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"af46262e-f13d-4ab6-811a-ccdebb35f12a"],
 " is the simplest knob on the distribution. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"T", " ", "=", " ", "0"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"89230c6a-9322-48ba-b659-320c3b0c1b36"],
 " is pure argmax (greedy); ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"T", " ", "=", " ", "1"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"50d16155-875f-40bc-a0bf-530a4a634d0d"],
 " is the model's calibrated distribution; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "1"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"2d80c091-8594-4045-a66e-f651f33a9672"],
 " softens toward uniform; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"T", 
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Rule]", " "}]}], "\[Infinity]"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"82648dc3-c87a-45e8-8d5f-c7b4240b0175"],
 " is exactly uniform."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d22f4bbe-03a8-48ee-b6bb-b6610901090e"],

Cell["Import[\"figures/temperature_sweep.png\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b6b6ef4c-92e4-498c-983c-f0d38b4b4478"],

Cell["2.1  Interactive: turn the temperature dial", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"c7e036a3-da44-40e8-8fad-e83455bb0a09"],

Cell["\<\
SeedRandom[3]; logits = Sort[RandomReal[NormalDistribution[0, 1.5], 20], \
Greater];
Manipulate[
  BarChart[
    LLMAtoZ`Sampling`softmaxTemperature[logits, T],
    Frame -> True, FrameLabel -> {\"token id\", \"probability\"},
    PlotLabel -> Row[{\"T = \", NumberForm[T, 3], \"  \[Bullet]  entropy = \
\",
      NumberForm[-Total[LLMAtoZ`Sampling`softmaxTemperature[logits, T] *
        Log[LLMAtoZ`Sampling`softmaxTemperature[logits, T] + 1.*^-12]], 3]}],
    PlotRange -> {Automatic, {0, 1}}, ChartStyle -> ColorData[97][1],
    ImageSize -> 500],
  {{T, 1.0, \"temperature\"}, 0.05, 3.0, 0.05, Appearance -> \"Labeled\"},
  ControlPlacement -> Top]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7da90c4a-2558-41f8-afd5-76002c6624fd"],

Cell["3.  Top-k and top-p (nucleus)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7027edf9-1444-4d14-a08b-e87f30887092"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Truncation strategies. ",
 StyleBox["Top-k",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " keeps the k highest-probability tokens and zeros the rest before ",
 "re-normalising. ",
 StyleBox["Top-p",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (nucleus sampling) instead keeps the smallest set of top tokens ",
 "whose cumulative probability exceeds ",
 Cell[BoxData["p"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"35e0ed91-b07c-4ac3-b6ef-d7fecc457975"],
 "; this adapts the cutoff to the local sharpness of the ",
 "distribution."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8269106f-5513-4f06-a22a-10f607be3a14"],

Cell["Import[\"figures/topk_vs_topp.png\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c87ce398-c3c5-4045-b19c-80d0fd38f1fb"],

Cell["4.  Beam search", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"531e9c22-2960-42ce-8aee-3b4b97131f0f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For translation-style tasks where one answer is correct, beam ",
 "search is the deterministic alternative: track the ",
 StyleBox["beamWidth",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " most likely partial sequences at every step, and at the end ",
 "return the highest-scoring complete one."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8a034bf4-9cb9-47c7-abd7-e031dd3348e4"],

Cell["\<\
(* Demo: beam search on a tiny 4-token problem.
   We define a fake stepFn that just returns scores based on the
   sequence so far -- enough to see beam search pick the best path. *)
fakeStep[ids_] := Module[{n = Length[ids]},
  RandomReal[NormalDistribution[0, 1], 6] +
    Table[If[i == Mod[n, 6] + 1, 2.0, 0.0], {i, 6}]];
SeedRandom[1];
LLMAtoZ`Sampling`beamSearch[fakeStep, {1}, 3, 8]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cd17f386-b2c5-4850-8c96-2478feb65c88"],

Cell["5.  Speculative decoding", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4d732aed-f392-4db5-9a0d-d1da56528e78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A small draft model proposes ",
 Cell[BoxData["k"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"4250596f-3c71-4b8f-ab14-0ff9dd2a9686"],
 " tokens autoregressively; the main model checks them in ",
 "a single forward pass; accepted tokens commit, the first rejected ",
 "token is resampled from the main. The throughput gain is roughly the ",
 "expected accept-length divided by (1 + draft_cost_ratio * k).  Useful ",
 "when the draft is much cheaper than the main."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"94583eed-dda8-47b7-8f56-6103f4995b08"],

Cell["Import[\"figures/speculative_throughput.png\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d3fac019-b1f3-4d81-b60f-0acbe5f27060"],

Cell["6.  Summary and what comes next", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e640b792-8290-46e3-9995-220925e71c74"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[FilledSquare] ",
 StyleBox["Five sampling strategies",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (greedy, temperature, top-k, top-p, beam) implemented from ",
 "scratch as one-liners or short functions over a length-|V| logit ",
 "vector.\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] ",
 StyleBox["Speculative decoding",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (Leviathan et al. 2023) for throughput speedup with a cheap ",
 "draft model.\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] ",
 StyleBox["An interactive temperature dial",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " showing the softmax distribution shape and entropy live."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8bef6162-a10c-4a4b-83cd-a1be6b379465"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In ",
 StyleBox["Part 6",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " we move from pre-training to ",
 StyleBox["supervised fine-tuning",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": same next-token loss, but on instruction-following data ",
 "formatted in the chat template <|user|>...<|assistant|>...<|eot|>."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"722bec22-41d3-43a4-b1ef-2e282af9b194"],

Cell["References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5cf57442-4d89-4bd7-8058-64d879a4b56c"],

Cell["\<\
Holtzman, A. et al. (2020). The Curious Case of Neural Text Degeneration. \
(Top-p / nucleus sampling.)
Leviathan, Y., Kalman, M., Matias, Y. (2023). Fast Inference from \
Transformers via Speculative Decoding.
Karpathy, A. (2025). nanochat.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1c16eb10-2647-4d28-837a-113a68121bd7"]
},
Saveable->True,
WindowSize->{900, 750},
